  steps:
    1. Pick odd side length N in {7,9,11,13}; set radius = N//2
    2. Choose background color bg (any color 0-9)
    3. Choose radius+1 distinct non-bg colors for rings 0..radius
    4. Build the output grid: fill each cell at Chebyshev distance d from center with color[d]
    5. Build the input grid: fill with bg, then for each distance d place one marker pixel with color[d] at a random cell whose Chebyshev distance from center is d
